{# ============================================================
   Five-column comparison
   ============================================================ #}
<div class="row">
    <div class="col-sm-12">
        <div class="compare-grid">

            {# Rationale — spans the left three columns; each block is
               aligned beside the schedule region it affects by the
               script at the foot of the page (data-anchor-for ↔ data-anchor). #}
            <div class="compare-col rationale-col">
                <div class="rationale-block" data-anchor-for="req-prog">
                    <h3 class="rationale-col__head">One schedule for everyone</h3>
                    <p>
                        The concern is that minor students may be behind — but you can't teach an
                        intro-to-programming course inside an intro-to-AI course. We actually don't
                        even require Data Structures outselves, it's just Fund Comp. If students can
                        get exposure from a revamped EG 10118 to basic python programming techniques and
                        programmatic thinking: with basic data structures (dicts,
                        lists) and control flow (loops, functions), they'll be completely fine. Our
                        majors won't have seen Jupyter, pandas, scikit-learn, or PyTorch either —
                        and those are the explicit focus of the labs — so while majors may have
                        slightly more programming experience, I really don't think the gap will make
                        much of a difference. At the end of the day this isn't really a programming
                        course, and the labs will help everyone.
                    </p>
                    <div class="rationale-topics">
                        <div class="rationale-topics__label">EG 10118 topics</div>
                        <div class="topic-cols">
                            <div class="topic-col">
                                <div class="topic-col__head">Must have</div>
                                <ul>
                                    <li>variables</li>
                                    <li>lists</li>
                                    <li>dicts</li>
                                    <li>conditionals</li>
                                    <li>loops</li>
                                    <li>functions</li>
                                </ul>
                            </div>
                            <div class="topic-col">
                                <div class="topic-col__head">Nice to have</div>
                                <ul>
                                    <li>classes</li>
                                    <li>a slightly harder problem (e.g. BFS / DFS)</li>
                                </ul>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="rationale-block" data-anchor-for="req-math">
                    <h3 class="rationale-col__head">Prerequisites &amp; co-requisites</h3>
                    <p>
                        I know it's an unpopular opinion, but I'm genuinely not convinced that either
                        statistics or linear algebra is required to get a conceptual handle on matrix
                        multiplication or distributions. An ML-focused, retooled prob-stats course
                        would obviously be useful as a co-requisite — but ultimately I think students
                        are better served by taking AI <em>earlier</em> than by any enrichment they'd
                        get from another semester of math beforehand, especially given the current
                        job and internship market. We don't even require Prob/Stats currently, just Linear.
                    </p>
                </div>

                <div class="rationale-block" data-anchor-for="gofai">
                    <h3 class="rationale-col__head">Dropping GOFAI</h3>
                    <p>
                        Broadly, I'm in favor of dropping GOFAI almost entirely. I didn't read your
                        full notes before drafting the schedule, but we both started with k-Nearest
                        Neighbors, so that's probably the natural place to begin. The GOFAI material
                        can be historically interesting and fun trivia, but it's fundamentally
                        different from modern learning algorithms, and students won't be missing
                        anything AI-wise without it — from an employability standpoint, if not
                        necessarily an idealized-education one. I struggle to see any real
                        application of the ~4 GOFAI lectures to downstream courses.
                    </p>
                </div>
            </div>

            {# Current schedule — paired with proposed in the right two columns #}
            <div class="compare-col">
                <div class="prereq-note" data-anchor="req-prog">
                    <div class="prereq-note__row">
                        <span class="prereq-note__tag">Pre-Req</span>
                        <span class="prereq-note__code">CSE 20311</span>
                    </div>
                    <div class="prereq-note__title">Fundamentals of Computing</div>
                </div>
                <div class="prereq-note" data-anchor="req-math">
                    <div class="prereq-note__row">
                        <span class="prereq-note__tag">Pre-Req</span>
                        <span class="prereq-note__code">MATH 20580</span>
                    </div>
                    <div class="prereq-note__title">Intro to Linear Algebra and DiffEq</div>
                </div>
                {{ currentScheduleBlock | safe }}
            </div>

            {# Proposed schedule #}
            <div class="compare-col">
                <div class="prereq-note">
                    <div class="prereq-note__row">
                        <span class="prereq-note__tag">Pre-Req</span>
                        <span class="prereq-note__code">EG 10118</span>
                    </div>
                    <div class="prereq-note__title">Engineering Computing in Python</div>
                </div>
                <div class="prereq-note">
                    <div class="prereq-note__row">
                        <span class="prereq-note__tag">Co-Req</span>
                        <span class="prereq-note__code">ACMS 30440</span>
                    </div>
                    <div class="prereq-note__title">Probability and Statistics for Machine Learning</div>
                </div>
                {{ proposedScheduleBlock | safe }}
            </div>

        </div>{# /compare-grid #}
    </div>{# /col-sm-12 #}
</div>{# /row #}

{# ============================================================
   Page behavior:
   1. Align each rationale block beside the schedule region it
      affects (wide screens only) via data-anchor-for ↔ data-anchor.
   2. Draw elbow connector arrows from each combined "current"
      lecture (data-split) to its "split" lectures in the proposed
      schedule (data-split-to), color-coded, with hover highlight.
   Both fall back gracefully on narrow screens / no-JS.
   ============================================================ #}
<script>
(function () {
    'use strict';
    var grid = document.querySelector('.compare-grid');
    if (!grid) return;
    var col = grid.querySelector('.rationale-col');

    /* ---------- 1. Rationale block alignment ---------- */
    var blocks = col ? Array.prototype.slice.call(col.querySelectorAll('.rationale-block')) : [];
    var alignMq = window.matchMedia('(min-width: 1101px)');
    var BLOCK_GAP = 26;

    function alignBlocks() {
        if (col) {
            col.style.position = '';
            col.style.minHeight = '';
            blocks.forEach(function (b) {
                b.style.position = ''; b.style.top = ''; b.style.left = ''; b.style.right = '';
            });
        }
        if (!col || !blocks.length || !alignMq.matches) return;
        var gridTop = grid.getBoundingClientRect().top;
        var items = blocks.map(function (b) {
            var key = b.getAttribute('data-anchor-for');
            var row = key && grid.querySelector('[data-anchor="' + key + '"]');
            var top = row ? row.getBoundingClientRect().top - gridTop : 0;
            return { el: b, top: Math.max(0, top) };
        }).sort(function (a, b) { return a.top - b.top; });
        col.style.position = 'relative';
        var cursor = 0;
        items.forEach(function (it) {
            var top = Math.max(it.top, cursor);
            it.el.style.position = 'absolute';
            it.el.style.left = '0';
            it.el.style.right = '0';
            it.el.style.top = top + 'px';
            cursor = top + it.el.offsetHeight + BLOCK_GAP;
        });
        col.style.minHeight = cursor + 'px';
    }

    /* ---------- 2. Split connector arrows ---------- */
    var SVGNS = 'http://www.w3.org/2000/svg';
    var COLORS = {
        dtree: '#c0392b', linreg: '#2980b9', logreg: '#27ae60', cluster: '#8e44ad',
        practicum: '#d35400', backprop: '#16a085', rnn: '#c2185b', attention: '#00838f',
        rl: '#3949ab', llm: '#6d4c41'
    };
    var sources = Array.prototype.slice.call(grid.querySelectorAll('[data-split]'));

    // Colors for the rationale brace ↔ requirement connectors.
    var BRACE_COLORS = {
        'req-prog': '#2e7d32',  // green — One schedule for everyone
        'req-math': '#6a1b9a',  // purple — Prerequisites & co-requisites
        'gofai': '#c62828'      // red — Dropping GOFAI
    };

    function makeDot(color, cls) {
        var d = document.createElement('span');
        d.className = 'split-dot ' + cls;
        d.style.backgroundColor = color;
        return d;
    }
    function createDots() {
        sources.forEach(function (src) {
            var key = src.getAttribute('data-split');
            var cell = src.children[src.children.length - 1];
            if (cell && !cell.querySelector('.split-dot--source')) {
                cell.appendChild(makeDot(COLORS[key] || '#b18d03', 'split-dot--source'));
            }
        });
        Array.prototype.forEach.call(grid.querySelectorAll('[data-split-to]'), function (tg) {
            var key = tg.getAttribute('data-split-to');
            var cell = tg.children[0]; // number cell — dot goes left of the number
            if (cell && !cell.querySelector('.split-dot--target')) {
                cell.insertBefore(makeDot(COLORS[key] || '#b18d03', 'split-dot--target'), cell.firstChild);
            }
        });
    }
    function center(el, gr, axis) {
        var r = el.getBoundingClientRect();
        return axis === 'x' ? (r.left + r.width / 2 - gr.left) : (r.top + r.height / 2 - gr.top);
    }

    function drawArrows() {
        var old = grid.querySelector('.split-arrows');
        if (old) old.parentNode.removeChild(old);
        if (window.innerWidth <= 680 || !sources.length) return;

        var gr = grid.getBoundingClientRect();
        var svg = document.createElementNS(SVGNS, 'svg');
        svg.setAttribute('class', 'split-arrows');
        svg.setAttribute('width', gr.width);
        svg.setAttribute('height', gr.height);

        var n = sources.length;
        sources.forEach(function (src, gi) {
            var key = src.getAttribute('data-split');
            var color = COLORS[key] || '#b18d03';
            var sdot = src.querySelector('.split-dot--source');
            if (!sdot) return;
            var x0 = center(sdot, gr, 'x');
            var ys = center(sdot, gr, 'y');
            var srcRight = src.getBoundingClientRect().right - gr.left;
            var targets = Array.prototype.slice.call(grid.querySelectorAll('[data-split-to="' + key + '"]'));
            if (!targets.length) return;
            var propLeft = targets[0].getBoundingClientRect().left - gr.left;
            // Each group's vertical trunk gets its own x within the channel.
            var xt = srcRight + (propLeft - srcRight) * (gi + 1) / (n + 1);
            targets.forEach(function (tg) {
                var tdot = tg.querySelector('.split-dot--target');
                if (!tdot) return;
                var xend = center(tdot, gr, 'x');
                var yt = center(tdot, gr, 'y');
                var path = document.createElementNS(SVGNS, 'path');
                path.setAttribute('class', 'split-arrow');
                path.setAttribute('d', 'M ' + x0 + ' ' + ys + ' H ' + xt + ' V ' + yt + ' H ' + xend);
                path.setAttribute('stroke', color);
                path.setAttribute('stroke-width', '1.4');
                path.setAttribute('stroke-opacity', '0.6');
                path.setAttribute('data-group', key);
                svg.appendChild(path);
            });
        });

        // Curly brace around each rationale block, prong pointing toward
        // the schedule region it applies to. Only when blocks are aligned
        // beside the schedules (wide layout).
        if (alignMq.matches && col) {
            blocks.forEach(function (b) {
                var key = b.getAttribute('data-anchor-for');
                var anchor = key && grid.querySelector('[data-anchor="' + key + '"]');
                if (!anchor) return;
                var br = b.getBoundingClientRect();
                var yT = br.top - gr.top;
                var yB = br.bottom - gr.top;
                var bx = (br.right - gr.left) + 5;   // arm tips, just past the block
                var xs = bx + 9;                     // spine
                var tx = xs + 13;                    // prong tip, toward schedule
                var r = 7;
                var ar = anchor.getBoundingClientRect();
                var aCenter = ar.top - gr.top + ar.height / 2;
                // Prong points at the anchor block, clamped into the brace's
                // span so it leans toward the target it refers to.
                var ty = Math.max(yT + 2 * r, Math.min(yB - 2 * r, aCenter));
                var d = 'M ' + bx + ' ' + yT +
                        ' Q ' + xs + ' ' + yT + ' ' + xs + ' ' + (yT + r) +
                        ' L ' + xs + ' ' + (ty - r) +
                        ' Q ' + xs + ' ' + ty + ' ' + tx + ' ' + ty +
                        ' Q ' + xs + ' ' + ty + ' ' + xs + ' ' + (ty + r) +
                        ' L ' + xs + ' ' + (yB - r) +
                        ' Q ' + xs + ' ' + yB + ' ' + bx + ' ' + yB;
                var bcolor = BRACE_COLORS[key] || 'rgba(0, 43, 92, 0.45)';
                var brace = document.createElementNS(SVGNS, 'path');
                brace.setAttribute('class', 'rationale-brace');
                brace.setAttribute('d', d);
                brace.style.stroke = bcolor;
                svg.appendChild(brace);

                // Draw a mirrored "{" brace hugging the target and a solid
                // connector joining the two brace prongs. The target is either
                // a requirement block, or a marked group of schedule rows
                // (e.g. the dropped GOFAI lectures).
                var tgt = null;
                if (anchor.classList && anchor.classList.contains('prereq-note')) {
                    tgt = { top: ar.top - gr.top, bottom: ar.bottom - gr.top, left: ar.left - gr.left };
                } else {
                    var grp = grid.querySelectorAll('[data-anchor-group="' + key + '"]');
                    if (grp.length) {
                        var gT = Infinity, gB = -Infinity, gL = Infinity;
                        Array.prototype.forEach.call(grp, function (el) {
                            var er = el.getBoundingClientRect();
                            gT = Math.min(gT, er.top - gr.top);
                            gB = Math.max(gB, er.bottom - gr.top);
                            gL = Math.min(gL, er.left - gr.left);
                        });
                        tgt = { top: gT, bottom: gB, left: gL };
                    }
                }
                if (tgt) {
                    var aLeft = tgt.left;
                    var aTop = tgt.top;
                    var aBot = tgt.bottom;
                    var tyr = (aTop + aBot) / 2;
                    var bxR = aLeft - 4;   // arms, hugging the target's left side
                    var xsR = bxR - 9;     // spine
                    var txR = xsR - 13;    // prong tip, pointing left
                    var rr = 6;
                    var dReq = 'M ' + bxR + ' ' + aTop +
                        ' Q ' + xsR + ' ' + aTop + ' ' + xsR + ' ' + (aTop + rr) +
                        ' L ' + xsR + ' ' + (tyr - rr) +
                        ' Q ' + xsR + ' ' + tyr + ' ' + txR + ' ' + tyr +
                        ' Q ' + xsR + ' ' + tyr + ' ' + xsR + ' ' + (tyr + rr) +
                        ' L ' + xsR + ' ' + (aBot - rr) +
                        ' Q ' + xsR + ' ' + aBot + ' ' + bxR + ' ' + aBot;
                    var reqBrace = document.createElementNS(SVGNS, 'path');
                    reqBrace.setAttribute('class', 'rationale-brace');
                    reqBrace.setAttribute('d', dReq);
                    reqBrace.style.stroke = bcolor;
                    svg.appendChild(reqBrace);

                    var conn = document.createElementNS(SVGNS, 'path');
                    conn.setAttribute('class', 'req-connector');
                    conn.setAttribute('d', 'M ' + tx + ' ' + ty + ' V ' + tyr + ' H ' + txR);
                    conn.style.stroke = bcolor;
                    svg.appendChild(conn);
                }
            });

            // Thin separators in the gaps between consecutive rationale blocks.
            var ordered = blocks.map(function (b) {
                var r2 = b.getBoundingClientRect();
                return { top: r2.top - gr.top, bottom: r2.bottom - gr.top, left: r2.left - gr.left, right: r2.right - gr.left };
            }).sort(function (a, b) { return a.top - b.top; });
            for (var si = 0; si < ordered.length - 1; si++) {
                var sepY = (ordered[si].bottom + ordered[si + 1].top) / 2;
                var sep = document.createElementNS(SVGNS, 'line');
                sep.setAttribute('class', 'rationale-sep');
                sep.setAttribute('x1', ordered[si].left);
                sep.setAttribute('y1', sepY);
                sep.setAttribute('x2', ordered[si].right);
                sep.setAttribute('y2', sepY);
                svg.appendChild(sep);
            }
        }

        grid.appendChild(svg);
    }

    /* ---------- hover highlight of a single split group ---------- */
    function highlight(key, on) {
        var svg = grid.querySelector('.split-arrows');
        if (svg) {
            svg.classList.toggle('is-dimmed', on);
            Array.prototype.forEach.call(svg.querySelectorAll('[data-group]'), function (el) {
                el.classList.toggle('is-active', on && el.getAttribute('data-group') === key);
            });
        }
        Array.prototype.forEach.call(
            grid.querySelectorAll('[data-split="' + key + '"], [data-split-to="' + key + '"]'),
            function (row) { row.classList.toggle('is-split-active', on); }
        );
    }
    function bindHover() {
        Array.prototype.forEach.call(grid.querySelectorAll('[data-split], [data-split-to]'), function (row) {
            var key = row.getAttribute('data-split') || row.getAttribute('data-split-to');
            row.addEventListener('mouseenter', function () { highlight(key, true); });
            row.addEventListener('mouseleave', function () { highlight(key, false); });
        });
    }

    function render() { alignBlocks(); drawArrows(); }
    function schedule() { window.requestAnimationFrame(render); }

    createDots();
    bindHover();
    window.addEventListener('load', schedule);
    window.addEventListener('resize', schedule);
    if (alignMq.addEventListener) { alignMq.addEventListener('change', schedule); }
    if (document.readyState === 'complete') { schedule(); }
})();
</script>
